+    <div class="grid grid-3" id="mentorsGrid">
+      <article class="card mentor-card" id="banio-luiji-nobert" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
+        <img class="mentor-photo" src="founder-banio.jpg" alt="Banio Luiji Nobert, Founder and Team Leader, Potential Unexplored Ltd, mentor at Boys to Men Mentorship Camp" loading="lazy" width="400" height="300" onerror="this.outerHTML='<div class=&quot;mentor-photo placeholder&quot;>BN</div>'">
+        <h3 itemprop="name">Banio Luiji Nobert</h3>
+        <p class="pill" itemprop="jobTitle">Founder and Team Leader, Potential Unexplored Ltd | Lead Facilitator</p>
+        <div class="bio-clamp"><p>Banio Luiji Nobert is the vision bearer of the Boys to Men Mentorship Program, an initiative of Potential Unexplored Ltd, where he leads a team of staff working to catalyse the rise of leaders who can effectively lead themselves and lead others.</p><p>He believes every great leader begins with one fundamental responsibility: learning to lead oneself, and then eventually leading others. He defines leadership as the ability to demonstrate a vision in words and action that positively affects the thoughts, feelings, and actions of oneself and other people, so that even if you did not require others to, they would still want to follow you.</p><p>Banio works from the conviction that leadership has two essential dimensions: self-leadership and people leadership. Self-leadership is the foundation, the ability to understand who we are, what we value, why we exist, and the potential within us. People who lead themselves well become grounded, intentional, and responsible, taking ownership of their thoughts, choices, habits, relationships, finances, and character.</p><p>People leadership is the next level: learning how to lead others, whether in a family, a team, an organisation, or a community. Great people leaders do not simply manage tasks. They build trust, create healthy relationships, encourage open communication, handle conflict constructively, develop commitment, and strengthen accountability.</p><p>As a corporate trainer and speaker, Nobert has made a name for Potential Unexplored across two fronts: organisational strengthening through leadership development, team building, and sales training, and life readiness programmes for young people and adults across Uganda and Africa.</p><p>Over more than a decade, Banio has trained, coached, and mentored individuals and teams across Uganda and Africa, with a client portfolio of more than fifty institutions including UNHCR, Bank of Uganda, Centenary Bank, War Child Canada, CORDAID South Sudan, Mastercard Foundation Scholars programme, horizont3000, and Opportunity International. He coordinated the Enabling Rural Innovation Programme across East Africa for five years and holds GALS Master Trainer and ERI Approach Global Quality Controller certifications. He is the author of twelve books, including The Team Accountability Compass and Heal to Lead.</p><p>He has led the development of a specialized training manual that covers all key sessions within the camp, making it easier for the scaling of the program across Africa and beyond.</p></div>
+        
+        <button class="read-more-btn" type="button">Read full profile</button>
+        <div class="mentor-jump-links">
+          <a href="#alionzi-lawrence-dangote">Next mentor: Alionzi Lawrence Dangote &rarr;</a>
+          <a href="#mentorsGrid">Back to all mentors</a>
+        </div>
+      </article>
+      <article class="card mentor-card" id="alionzi-lawrence-dangote" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
+        <img class="mentor-photo" src="mentor-alionzi-dangote.jpg" alt="Alionzi Lawrence Dangote, Mayor, Arua City 2026&ndash;2031, mentor at Boys to Men Mentorship Camp" loading="lazy" width="400" height="300" onerror="this.outerHTML='<div class=&quot;mentor-photo placeholder&quot;>AD</div>'">
+        <h3 itemprop="name">Alionzi Lawrence Dangote</h3>
+        <p class="pill" itemprop="jobTitle">Mayor, Arua City 2026&ndash;2031 | 88th Guild President, Makerere University | Electrical Engineer</p>
+        <div class="bio-clamp"><p>The youngest City Mayor in Uganda leading Arua City in West Nile, Lawrence's story is one of the most striking any boy at camp usually hears. Born and raised in West Nile, Dangote rose to become the 88th Guild President of Makerere University, Uganda's oldest and most prestigious institution of higher learning, where he pursued engineering. Upon graduation, he served as Managing Director of Joadah Design Institute.</p><p>To have reached elected office at the age of 26 years, in a role most people spend decades working toward, makes Lawrence a living example of what is possible when leadership is taken seriously early. He has spoken to boys at camp about public speaking and leadership, drawing directly on his own path from student leader to engineer to the youngest mayor in Uganda, and pushing every boy in the room to see city hall, not as something distant, but as somewhere he could genuinely stand one day.</p></div>
+        
+        <button class="read-more-btn" type="button">Read full profile</button>
